# Navigation order for the subject taxonomy -- see about/our-taxonomy.md.
# Without this, awesome-pages sorts alphabetically and opens the site on
# christian-life, scattering the doctrinal teaching order.
nav:
  - index.md
  - scripture
  - god
  - jesus
  - biblical-figures
  - spiritual-beings
  - sin
  - salvation
  - israel-and-church
  - last-things
  - feasts
  - christian-life
  - commentaries
  - sermons
  - resources
  # A lookup surface rather than a section: short definitions that link out to the page
  # owning each term. Sits with the reference material, above the interactive tools.
  - glossary.md
  # All three interactive tools are ordinary mkdocs pages: a React bundle built by esbuild into
  # docs/content/assets/js/ is mounted into each. Astro is gone, so there is no second build and
  # no stitch step, and `mkdocs serve` renders them like any other page -- run `npm run build:tools`
  # in app/ first, or the mount div comes up empty.
  # Deliberately flat rather than nested under a "Tools" section: the theme's navigation.prune
  # feature renders a section that is never on the active path as one link to its first child,
  # which would have hidden the others entirely.
  # references.md leads: it is the one a reader reaches for while actually studying a passage.
  - references.md
  - timeline.md
  - genealogy.md
  - about
